    REFACTOR-0001: move the booking rules into the core
    
    src/bookings.ts did four jobs at once: read the file, decide whether a
    request breaks a rule, write the file, and word the answer. Only the
    second is about bookings.
    
    refusalFor() takes a request and the room's other bookings that day,
    and says why it can't be booked, or undefined if it can: the 2-hour
    limit and the overlap check, moved from src/bookings.ts. It's plain
    data in and plain data out. It reads the core's Booking, which calls
    the times start and end; what the file calls them is no longer the
    rules' business. Which bookings count as "the room's other bookings
    that day" is now the store's job, so the overlap check no longer
    compares rooms or dates.
    
    book() is the core's one use case. It asks the store for the room's
    bookings that day, asks refusalFor(), and adds the request if nothing
    refuses it. It only knows the store as a BookingStore.
    
    The tests in test/core/rooms.spec.ts pass. They use plain Booking
    objects and a FakeBookingStore, and none of them knows the file format.
    Nothing calls the core yet.

